This is the Atalla 0x01 Cycle Accurate Simulator.

The main website can be found at https://github.com/Purdue-SoCET/atalla/.

> This repository is currently being built. 

A good starting point is https://github.com/Purdue-SoCET/atalla/docs, and for
more information about building the simulator and getting started
please see https://github.com/Purdue-SoCET/Atalla-Sim/docs. 

The main source tree includes these subdirectories:
    /benchmarks/ -> Benchmarking kernels.
    /configs/ -> Design Configurations.
    /docs/ -> Documentation of Arch, Contribution Guide, etc.
    /src/ -> Core Design Files.
    /src/native/ -> Optional C++ SIMD kernels (AVX2 / AVX-512).
    /tests/ -> Unit Tests.
    /scripts/ -> CI/CD pipelines.
    /LICENSE
    /Makefile
    /README

BUILDING THE SIMD KERNELS
-------------------------

    make native

This compiles src/native/atalla_kernels.cpp into a shared object that
accelerates the systolic-array datapath and the fp16 cast. The build is
optional: without it the simulator runs a pure-numpy fallback that produces
bit-identical results, just more slowly. A single .so carries AVX-512F, AVX2
and portable scalar code paths and picks one at load time via CPUID, so it can
be built once and copied between machines.

Measured on a 32x32 fp16 array (Xeon E5-2697A v4, AVX2, no AVX-512):

    pure Python (previous)   2070 us / simulated cycle
    numpy fallback            400 us / simulated cycle
    native AVX2                80 us / simulated cycle    ~25x

Reproduce the last two with:

    python tools/bench_native.py

What remains after this is FIFO and event-queue bookkeeping, not arithmetic,
so a wider vector unit alone will not move the number much further.

To confirm which path is active, or to force the fallback:

    python3 -c "import sys; sys.path.insert(0,'src'); \
        from native import kernels; print(kernels.NATIVE_ISA)"
    ATALLA_NO_NATIVE=1 pytest tests/     # run without the .so

The kernels are held to bit-exact equivalence with the pure-Python reference:
no FMA (products are rounded before they are summed), double-precision
throughout, and lane reductions kept in their original left-to-right order.
tests/native/ checks the fp16 cast against numpy across every half-precision
midpoint and verifies the native and fallback datapaths tick identically.

If you have questions, please send mail to socet@purdue.edu.

Enjoy using Atalla-Sim and please share your modifications and extensions.

*NOTE!*

This project draws conceptual and structural inspiration from the
[gem5 Simulator](https://www.gem5.org/) project.

Many architectural ideas — including the modular class hierarchy, 
naming conventions, and simulation lifecycle — are based on the gem5 design.

gem5 is © The gem5 Project and distributed under the BSD 3-Clause License.